# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Full quantum state tomography of an $N$-qubit system requires exponentially many measurements to estimate all $4^N -1$ independent parameters of the density matrix. For a system of 50 qubits, for example, this process requires on the order of $10^{30}$ shots, which is more than a billion times the number of stars in the observable universe. Shadow tomography [\\[1\\]](#references) is a quantum information protocol that constructs a “classical shadow” of the quantum state, from which target observables can be estimated by using a number of shots that scales logarithmically in the number of observables and is independent of system size $N$, making it relevant across many areas in quantum computing, including energy estimation, entanglement entropy and correlation function calculations, kernel estimation in quantum machine learning, and others.\n"
msgstr "Tomografi state kuantum penuh pada sistem $N$-qubit membutuhkan pengukuran yang jumlahnya eksponensial untuk mengestimasi semua $4^N -1$ parameter independen dari matriks densitas. Untuk sistem 50 qubit, misalnya, proses ini membutuhkan sekitar $10^{30}$ shot, yang lebih dari satu miliar kali jumlah bintang di alam semesta teramati. Shadow tomography [\\[1\\]](#references) adalah protokol informasi kuantum yang membangun “classical shadow” dari state kuantum, yang darinya observabel target dapat diestimasi dengan jumlah shot yang berskala logaritmik terhadap jumlah observabel dan tidak bergantung pada ukuran sistem $N$, sehingga relevan di banyak bidang komputasi kuantum, termasuk estimasi energi, perhitungan entropi entanglement dan fungsi korelasi, estimasi kernel dalam machine learning kuantum, dan lainnya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This tutorial shows how to use shadow tomography to estimate local observables, such as the single-qubit magnetization $\\langle Z_i \\rangle$ for qubit $i$, the two-point correlation function $\\langle Z_i Z_j\\rangle$, and the two-qubit reduced density matrix (2-RDM), of the highly entangled Greenberger-Horne-Zeilinger (GHZ) state. The tutorial first illustrates a small-scale shadow tomography workflow on a 10-qubit GHZ state by using statevector simulation. Then it shows a 100-qubit demonstration on real quantum hardware.\n"
msgstr "Tutorial ini menunjukkan cara memakai shadow tomography untuk mengestimasi observabel lokal, seperti magnetisasi satu qubit $\\langle Z_i \\rangle$ untuk qubit $i$, fungsi korelasi dua titik $\\langle Z_i Z_j\\rangle$, dan matriks densitas tereduksi dua qubit (2-RDM), dari state Greenberger-Horne-Zeilinger (GHZ) yang sangat entangled. Tutorial ini pertama-tama mengilustrasikan alur kerja shadow tomography skala kecil pada state GHZ 10 qubit memakai simulasi statevector. Lalu ia menunjukkan demonstrasi 100 qubit pada hardware kuantum sungguhan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Shadow tomography protocol {#shadow-tomography-protocol}"
msgstr "Protokol shadow tomography {#shadow-tomography-protocol}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The shadow tomography protocol has the following steps:\n"
"1. Apply a random unitary $U$, drawn from a unitary ensemble, to the initial quantum state.\n"
"2. Measure the outcome in the computational basis, obtaining a bitstring $\\ket{b}$.\n"
"3. Store the classical snapshot, $\\hat{\\rho} = \\mathcal{M}^{-1}(U^{\\dagger}\\ket{b}\\bra{b}U)$, where $\\mathcal{M}^{-1}$ is the inverse of the measurement channel $\\mathcal{M}(\\rho)=\\mathbb{E}[U^{\\dagger}\\ket{b}\\bra{b}U]$.\n"
"4. Repeat the process $T$ times, where the collection of $T$ snapshots $\\{\\hat{\\rho}_t\\}$ forms a classical shadow $S(\\rho, T)$.\n"
"5. Estimate observable $o$ of operator $O$ as $\\frac{1}{T}\\sum_{t=1}^{T}\\text{Tr}(O\\hat{\\rho}_t)$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Protokol shadow tomography memiliki langkah-langkah berikut:\n"
"1. Terapkan unitari acak $U$, yang diambil dari sebuah ensemble unitari, ke state kuantum awal.\n"
"2. Ukur hasilnya dalam basis komputasi, sehingga diperoleh bitstring $\\ket{b}$.\n"
"3. Simpan snapshot klasik, $\\hat{\\rho} = \\mathcal{M}^{-1}(U^{\\dagger}\\ket{b}\\bra{b}U)$, dengan $\\mathcal{M}^{-1}$ adalah invers dari kanal pengukuran $\\mathcal{M}(\\rho)=\\mathbb{E}[U^{\\dagger}\\ket{b}\\bra{b}U]$.\n"
"4. Ulangi proses ini sebanyak $T$ kali, di mana kumpulan $T$ snapshot $\\{\\hat{\\rho}_t\\}$ membentuk classical shadow $S(\\rho, T)$.\n"
"5. Estimasi observabel $o$ dari operator $O$ sebagai $\\frac{1}{T}\\sum_{t=1}^{T}\\text{Tr}(O\\hat{\\rho}_t)$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Shadow tomography variants {#shadow-tomography-variants}"
msgstr "Varian shadow tomography {#shadow-tomography-variants}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The choice of the unitary ensemble, that is, basis, in step 1 of the protocol, affects the sample complexity, variance of estimates, and information completeness of a given shadow tomography. Many ensemble groups have been considered in the literature, each with trade-offs between complexity and observable estimation efficiency. The properties of the most commonly used variants are summarized in the following table, although this list is not exhaustive.\n"
msgstr "Pilihan ensemble unitari, yaitu basis, pada langkah 1 protokol memengaruhi kompleksitas sampel, varians estimasi, dan kelengkapan informasi dari suatu shadow tomography. Banyak grup ensemble telah dipertimbangkan dalam literatur, masing-masing dengan trade-off antara kompleksitas dan efisiensi estimasi observabel. Properti varian yang paling umum dipakai dirangkum dalam tabel berikut, meskipun daftar ini tidak lengkap.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Variant | Ensemble | Sample complexity | Circuit depth | Suitable observables |\n"
"| ------------ | ---------------------------------| ---------| ---| -------- |\n"
"| local Pauli [\\[1\\]](#references) | single-qubit Paulis $\\{X, Y, Z\\}$ | $\\mathcal{O}(3^k\\text{log}M/\\varepsilon^2)$ | 1 | local/few-body |\n"
"| global Clifford [\\[1\\]](#references) | $N$-qubit Clifford |$\\mathcal{O}(\\text{Tr}(O^2)\\text{log}M/\\varepsilon^2)$ | $\\mathcal{O}(N\\text{log}N)$ | low-rank, fidelity |\n"
"| fermionic Gaussian [\\[2\\]](#references), [\\[3\\]](#references)| matchgate circuits | $\\mathcal{O}(\\binom{\\mu}{k}\\frac{1}{\\varepsilon^2})$  | $\\mathcal{O}(N^2)$ | fermionic |\n"
"| shallow shadows [\\[4\\]](#references), [\\[5\\]](#references) | low-depth circuits| $\\mathcal{O}(k2^k\\text{log}M/\\varepsilon^2)$ | $\\mathcal{O}(\\text{log}N)$ | non-local (hardware-friendly) |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Varian | Ensemble | Kompleksitas sampel | Kedalaman circuit | Observabel yang cocok |\n"
"| ------------ | ---------------------------------| ---------| ---| -------- |\n"
"| Pauli lokal [\\[1\\]](#references) | Pauli satu qubit $\\{X, Y, Z\\}$ | $\\mathcal{O}(3^k\\text{log}M/\\varepsilon^2)$ | 1 | lokal/few-body |\n"
"| Clifford global [\\[1\\]](#references) | Clifford $N$-qubit |$\\mathcal{O}(\\text{Tr}(O^2)\\text{log}M/\\varepsilon^2)$ | $\\mathcal{O}(N\\text{log}N)$ | rank rendah, fidelitas |\n"
"| Gaussian fermionik [\\[2\\]](#references), [\\[3\\]](#references)| circuit matchgate | $\\mathcal{O}(\\binom{\\mu}{k}\\frac{1}{\\varepsilon^2})$  | $\\mathcal{O}(N^2)$ | fermionik |\n"
"| shallow shadows [\\[4\\]](#references), [\\[5\\]](#references) | circuit berkedalaman rendah| $\\mathcal{O}(k2^k\\text{log}M/\\varepsilon^2)$ | $\\mathcal{O}(\\text{log}N)$ | non-lokal (ramah hardware) |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The terms used in the table are defined as follows:\n"
msgstr "Istilah yang dipakai dalam tabel didefinisikan sebagai berikut:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "\"sample complexity\" refers to the number of measurements needed for a given shadow tomography variant.\n"
msgstr "\"kompleksitas sampel\" mengacu pada jumlah pengukuran yang dibutuhkan untuk suatu varian shadow tomography.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "\"circuit depth\" describes how expensive the measurements are to implement on quantum hardware.\n"
msgstr "\"kedalaman circuit\" menggambarkan seberapa mahal pengukuran untuk diimplementasikan pada hardware kuantum.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "$N$ is the number of qubits.\n"
msgstr "$N$ adalah jumlah qubit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "$k$ is the locality of the observable (for example, $\\langle Z_i \\rangle$ has $k=1$ and $\\langle Z_i Z_j\\rangle$ has $k=2$).\n"
msgstr "$k$ adalah lokalitas observabel (misalnya, $\\langle Z_i \\rangle$ punya $k=1$ dan $\\langle Z_i Z_j\\rangle$ punya $k=2$).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "$M$ is the number of observables to be estimated simultaneously.\n"
msgstr "$M$ adalah jumlah observabel yang diestimasi secara bersamaan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "$\\varepsilon$ is the additive error tolerance.\n"
msgstr "$\\varepsilon$ adalah toleransi error aditif.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "$\\mu$ is the number of fermions.\n"
msgstr "$\\mu$ adalah jumlah fermion.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Though the local Pauli ensemble is the most hardware-friendly, it pays a $3^k$ sample complexity penalty, which makes it ill-suited for non-local property estimation. More generally, the local-shadow sample-complexity bound scales as $4^k$, improving to $3^k$ in the special case of tensor-product observables.\n"
msgstr "Meskipun ensemble Pauli lokal paling ramah hardware, ia menanggung penalti kompleksitas sampel $3^k$, sehingga kurang cocok untuk estimasi properti non-lokal. Secara lebih umum, batas kompleksitas sampel local-shadow berskala $4^k$, membaik menjadi $3^k$ pada kasus khusus observabel hasil kali tensor.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Conversely, while the global Clifford ensemble can be used to estimate non-local observables, its circuit depth is not favorable. Fermionic Gaussian shadows offer utility in simulations of many-body physics, chemistry, and materials, but require matchgate circuits, which might carry significant overhead on general purpose gate-based devices.\n"
msgstr "Sebaliknya, meskipun ensemble Clifford global bisa dipakai untuk mengestimasi observabel non-lokal, kedalaman circuit-nya kurang menguntungkan. Shadow Gaussian fermionik berguna dalam simulasi fisika many-body, kimia, dan material, tetapi membutuhkan circuit matchgate, yang mungkin membawa overhead signifikan pada perangkat berbasis gate serbaguna.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Shallow shadows has a circuit depth between the local Pauli and global Clifford, making it a highly promising variant for practical implementation, though there are still some open questions regarding optimal circuit depth for a given observable.\n"
msgstr "Shallow shadows punya kedalaman circuit di antara Pauli lokal dan Clifford global, sehingga menjadi varian yang sangat menjanjikan untuk implementasi praktis, meskipun masih ada beberapa pertanyaan terbuka mengenai kedalaman circuit optimal untuk suatu observabel.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As the frontier of shadow tomography research continues expanding, some of the most relevant problems to address include optimally choosing the measurement ensemble for a target set of observables, improving sample complexity bounds, and extending the protocol to time-evolved observables. Nonetheless, shadow tomography still presents one of the leading workflows for extracting maximal classical information from a quantum state using a minimum number of measurements, which makes it ideal for characterizing quantum states at scale where both full tomography and classical simulation are impossible.\n"
msgstr "Seiring terus berkembangnya frontier riset shadow tomography, beberapa masalah paling relevan yang perlu ditangani mencakup pemilihan ensemble pengukuran yang optimal untuk himpunan observabel target, perbaikan batas kompleksitas sampel, dan perluasan protokol ke observabel yang berevolusi terhadap waktu. Meskipun demikian, shadow tomography tetap menjadi salah satu alur kerja terdepan untuk mengekstrak informasi klasik maksimal dari sebuah state kuantum dengan jumlah pengukuran minimum, sehingga ideal untuk mengkarakterisasi state kuantum pada skala di mana tomografi penuh maupun simulasi klasik tidak mungkin dilakukan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "The local Pauli ensemble {#the-local-pauli-ensemble}"
msgstr "Ensemble Pauli lokal {#the-local-pauli-ensemble}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This tutorial uses the random Pauli basis, that is, single-qubit Clifford gates, to collect shadows and estimate properties of the GHZ state. Note that the Pauli measurements are a great choice for estimating local observables (such as spin density, local correlation functions, and position probability density), but not global ones (such as total energy, momentum, and charge).\n"
msgstr "Tutorial ini memakai basis Pauli acak, yaitu gate Clifford satu qubit, untuk mengumpulkan shadow dan mengestimasi properti state GHZ. Perhatikan bahwa pengukuran Pauli adalah pilihan yang bagus untuk mengestimasi observabel lokal (seperti densitas spin, fungsi korelasi lokal, dan densitas probabilitas posisi), tetapi tidak untuk observabel global (seperti energi total, momentum, dan muatan).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here, a random Pauli basis $\\{X, Y, Z\\}$ per qubit is independently chosen and the corresponding single-qubit rotation is applied, followed by measurement:\n"
msgstr "Di sini, basis Pauli acak $\\{X, Y, Z\\}$ dipilih secara independen untuk setiap qubit dan rotasi satu qubit yang sesuai diterapkan, diikuti pengukuran:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$$\n"
msgstr "$$\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\begin{equation}\n"
"U = U_0 \\otimes U_1 \\otimes \\cdots \\otimes U_{n-1}, U_q \\in \\{I, H, S^{\\dagger}H\\}\n"
"\\end{equation}\n"
"\\tag{1}\n"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{equation}\n"
"U = U_0 \\otimes U_1 \\otimes \\cdots \\otimes U_{n-1}, U_q \\in \\{I, H, S^{\\dagger}H\\}\n"
"\\end{equation}\n"
"\\tag{1}\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For this ensemble, the measurement channel's inverse is:\n"
msgstr "Untuk ensemble ini, invers dari kanal pengukuran adalah:\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\begin{equation}\n"
"\\hat{\\rho}_q=3U_q^{\\dagger}\\ket{b_q}\\bra{b_q}U_q - I\n"
"\\end{equation}\n"
"\\tag{2}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{equation}\n"
"\\hat{\\rho}_q=3U_q^{\\dagger}\\ket{b_q}\\bra{b_q}U_q - I\n"
"\\end{equation}\n"
"\\tag{2}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The factor of $3$ comes from averaging over the three Pauli bases, which produces a depolarizing channel with parameter $\\frac{1}{3}$. The full estimator then factorizes as a product of single-qubit estimators. As shown in the table, for $M$ observables, each of locality $k$, the number of Pauli shadows needed to estimate all observables to additive error $\\varepsilon$ with high probability is $\\mathcal{O}(\\frac{3^k\\text{log}(M)}{\\varepsilon^2})$. The system size does not affect the measurement cost as long as the observables remain local, so exponentially many observables can be estimated simultaneously with only logarithmic cost.\n"
msgstr "Faktor $3$ berasal dari perataan atas tiga basis Pauli, yang menghasilkan kanal depolarisasi dengan parameter $\\frac{1}{3}$. Estimator penuhnya kemudian terfaktorisasi sebagai hasil kali estimator satu qubit. Seperti ditunjukkan dalam tabel, untuk $M$ observabel, masing-masing berlokalitas $k$, jumlah shadow Pauli yang dibutuhkan untuk mengestimasi semua observabel hingga error aditif $\\varepsilon$ dengan probabilitas tinggi adalah $\\mathcal{O}(\\frac{3^k\\text{log}(M)}{\\varepsilon^2})$. Ukuran sistem tidak memengaruhi biaya pengukuran selama observabelnya tetap lokal, sehingga observabel yang jumlahnya eksponensial dapat diestimasi sekaligus dengan biaya yang hanya logaritmik.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Median of means {#median-of-means}"
msgstr "Median of means {#median-of-means}"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A plain mean over $T$ snapshots reduces the variance of a single-shot estimate of an observable as $\\frac{1}{T}$, but is sensitive to outliers. Median of means can be used to remedy this. The process involves the following:\n"
"- Splitting the $T$ snapshots into $K$ equally-sized groups\n"
"- Computing the mean within each group\n"
"- Returning the median across group means\n"
msgstr ""
"Rata-rata biasa atas $T$ snapshot mengurangi varians dari estimasi satu-shot suatu observabel sebanding dengan $\\frac{1}{T}$, tetapi sensitif terhadap outlier. Median of means dapat dipakai untuk mengatasinya. Prosesnya meliputi:\n"
"- Membagi $T$ snapshot menjadi $K$ grup berukuran sama\n"
"- Menghitung rata-rata dalam setiap grup\n"
"- Mengembalikan median dari rata-rata grup\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
