# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Large-scale hardware example {#large-scale-hardware-example}"
msgstr "Contoh hardware skala besar {#large-scale-hardware-example}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The preceding simulation confirms that local Pauli shadow tomography recovers the correct observables on a noiseless statevector. Running the same protocol using 100 qubits on real hardware introduces two challenges that do not appear in simulation: gate and readout errors accumulate across the deep GHZ circuit, and finding the optimal qubit layout requires searching the device's coupling graph rather than choosing a layout by hand.\n"
msgstr "Simulasi sebelumnya mengonfirmasi bahwa local Pauli shadow tomography memulihkan observabel yang benar pada statevector tanpa noise. Menjalankan protokol yang sama dengan 100 qubit di hardware sungguhan menimbulkan dua tantangan yang tidak muncul di simulasi: error Gate dan readout menumpuk di sepanjang Circuit GHZ yang dalam, dan menemukan layout qubit yang optimal butuh pencarian di graf coupling perangkat, bukan memilih layout secara manual.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To address the first challenge, use low-overhead error detection with spacetime codes [[6]](#references). A small number of ancilla qubits adjacent to the GHZ tree are used as parity checks. Each ancilla is entangled with two of its GHZ neighbors before measurement, so a single bit-flip error on either neighbor flips the ancilla's outcome from `0` to `1`. Snapshots where any check ancilla reads `1` are discarded, leaving a cleaner subset from which to estimate $\\langle Z_i Z_{i+1}\\rangle$.\n"
msgstr "Untuk mengatasi tantangan pertama, gunakan deteksi error dengan overhead rendah memakai spacetime codes [[6]](#references). Sejumlah kecil qubit ancilla yang bersebelahan dengan pohon GHZ dipakai sebagai parity check. Tiap ancilla di-entangle dengan dua tetangganya di GHZ sebelum diukur, sehingga satu bit-flip error pada salah satu tetangga membalik hasil ancilla dari `0` menjadi `1`. Snapshot yang punya ancilla pemeriksa bernilai `1` dibuang, menyisakan subset yang lebih bersih untuk memperkirakan $\\langle Z_i Z_{i+1}\\rangle$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The second challenge is handled by searching over candidate GHZ tree layouts and selecting the one that maximizes parity-check coverage, that is, the fraction of circuit wires monitored by at least one check, within an acceptable increase in circuit depth.\n"
msgstr "Tantangan kedua diatasi dengan mencari berbagai kandidat layout pohon GHZ lalu memilih yang memaksimalkan cakupan parity-check, yaitu fraksi wire Circuit yang dipantau oleh setidaknya satu pemeriksa, dengan kenaikan kedalaman Circuit yang masih dapat diterima.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Steps 1-4 (performed in a single code block) {#steps-1-4-performed-in-a-single-code-block}"
msgstr "Langkah 1-4 (dijalankan dalam satu blok kode) {#steps-1-4-performed-in-a-single-code-block}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The same four-step workflow is now applied to a 100-qubit GHZ state on real quantum hardware, adding two hardware-specific features that do not arise in simulation:\n"
msgstr "Alur kerja empat langkah yang sama sekarang diterapkan ke state GHZ 100-qubit di hardware kuantum sungguhan, dengan menambahkan dua fitur khusus hardware yang tidak muncul di simulasi:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Step 1** characterizes the backend noise (gate errors, readout errors, and T2 times) so that unreliable qubits and edges are excluded from the circuit layout.\n"
msgstr "**Langkah 1** mengkarakterisasi noise Backend (error Gate, error readout, dan waktu T2) supaya qubit dan edge yang tidak andal dikeluarkan dari layout Circuit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Step 2** searches over possible GHZ tree layouts to find one that maximizes parity-check coverage within an acceptable circuit depth — replacing the trivial chain used in simulation.\n"
msgstr "**Langkah 2** mencari berbagai layout pohon GHZ untuk menemukan yang memaksimalkan cakupan parity-check dalam kedalaman Circuit yang masih dapat diterima, menggantikan rantai sederhana yang dipakai di simulasi.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Step 3** builds the shadow circuits (one per random Pauli basis), transpiles them to hardware-native gates, and submits them to the Sampler primitive with `shots=8` (each circuit produces eight independent bitstrings).\n"
msgstr "**Langkah 3** membangun Circuit shadow (satu per basis Pauli acak), men-transpile-nya ke Gate native hardware, dan mengirimkannya ke primitive Sampler dengan `shots=8` (tiap Circuit menghasilkan delapan bitstring independen).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Step 4** postselects snapshots whose check qubits all read 0 (no detected error), then estimates $\\langle Z_i Z_{i+1}\\rangle$ with and without that postselection to demonstrate the improvement from error detection.\n"
msgstr "**Langkah 4** melakukan postselect pada snapshot yang semua qubit pemeriksanya bernilai 0 (tidak ada error terdeteksi), lalu memperkirakan $\\langle Z_i Z_{i+1}\\rangle$ dengan dan tanpa postselection tersebut untuk menunjukkan peningkatan dari deteksi error.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/shadow-tomography/extracted-outputs/502e92dd-1.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/shadow-tomography/extracted-outputs/502e92dd-1.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Interpret the results {#interpret-the-results}"
msgstr "Menafsirkan hasil {#interpret-the-results}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The two plots show $\\langle Z_i Z_{i+1}\\rangle$ estimated from shadow tomography for each neighboring qubit pair in the 100-qubit GHZ chain, before and after postselecting on the parity checks.\n"
msgstr "Kedua plot menunjukkan $\\langle Z_i Z_{i+1}\\rangle$ hasil estimasi shadow tomography untuk setiap pasangan qubit bertetangga di rantai GHZ 100-qubit, sebelum dan sesudah postselection pada parity check.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For an ideal GHZ state, all nearest-neighbor correlators equal $1$. On hardware, noise depresses the raw estimates and introduces qubit-to-qubit scatter. After error detection, snapshots in which at least one detectable error occurred are removed, and the remaining estimates are pulled closer to $1$ with reduced variance, which is consistent with a cleaner effective state.\n"
msgstr "Untuk state GHZ ideal, semua korelator tetangga terdekat bernilai $1$. Di hardware, noise menurunkan estimasi mentah dan menimbulkan sebaran antar qubit. Setelah deteksi error, snapshot yang mengandung setidaknya satu error terdeteksi dibuang, dan estimasi yang tersisa bergeser lebih dekat ke $1$ dengan varians lebih kecil, yang sesuai dengan state efektif yang lebih bersih.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The improvement after error detection is consistent with the checks detecting real errors.\n"
msgstr "Peningkatan setelah deteksi error sesuai dengan pemeriksa yang mendeteksi error sungguhan.\n"

